              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "suzanna"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Vinegar, vinegar, vinegar! I reduced the vinegar before I made it because it seemed like a suspiciously high amount, and it was still pretty much inedible. I cooked it for 3 hours hoping to cook some of the vinegar off. Nope. It was pickled cherries. I did think the Chinese Five Spice was a good shortcut seasoning, but Garam Masala would be much more authentic.",
